secubox-yacy (1.0.13-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * SECURITY vhost: restrict the YaCy admin surface (Status, Config*, Network,
    Performance*, Settings*, ViewLog, Table_*, Index*, Crawl*, …) to internal
    zones. The vhost is publicly routed and YaCy only authenticates its `_p`
    pages, so node state, base configuration and peer topology were readable
    from the Internet. The search portal (/, /index.html, /yacysearch*,
    /suggest.json, /env/*) stays public — YaCy admin pages are CamelCase, the
    portal ones are not, so the regex does not touch them.
  * The allow-list names zones (LAN, lan3, br-lxc, wg-admin) instead of opening
    all of 10.0.0.0/8 like the exposure snippets do: wg-toolbox (browsing
    clients) and wg-mesh (other boxes) have no business reading this node's
    configuration. (ref #941)

